    <GaugingStation location="Crabbs Bridge" name="Ter" number="37003">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Long period of record from a rural catchment, includes daily flow record of a former, less accurate station Hatfield Peverel.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Theoretically rated. Modular limit ~0.2m, depending on downstream weed, no level yet recorded above 1.6m (structurefull). Scatter in gaugings beyond QMED caused by drowning. One peak flow rating applied across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Trapezoidal flume with throat tapping and low flow control, replaced less accurate station - Hatfield Peverel, 900m d/s, in 1964. Hatfield Peverel record held with this station (1932-1964).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">No POT data are presented for this station as they have no non-modular flow correction applied. AMAX data have been corrected. Records in 1932-1964 are from a former, less accurate Hatfield Peverel station. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Minor surface water abstractions for spray irrigation, small discharges from STW but net export through PWS.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">London Clay, overlain with superficial deposits, mainly Boulder Clay and some sands and gravels. Rural, predominantly arable land.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">PI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED. Rating accounts for drowning." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Many AMAX events are out of bank, and the rating makes no allowance for out of bank flow. Also, some spot gaugings show scatter from the rating." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
